- activate_origin_node: parameters (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
  precondition: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, not origin_node_ready ?origin_node, not origin_node_occupied ?origin_node.
  effect: origin_node_ready ?origin_node.

Thus to activate origin node we need origin_availability prepared and task profile linked, and origin availability node linked (we have that), and node not ready/occupied (currently origin_node_alpha not ready nor occupied). So we need to prepare origin_availability_alpha and link task profile.

- lock_origin_availability: parameters (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?operator_resource - operator_resource)
  precondition: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, origin_node_ready ?origin_node, not origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability.
  effect: origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability.

Thus after we have origin availability prepared, operator linked, node ready, we can lock it (which also confirms).

- load_origin_payload: parameters (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?payload_unit - cargo_payload)
  precondition: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, cargo_available ?payload_unit, not origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability.
  effect: origin_node_occupied ?origin_node, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, origin_payload_linked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit, not cargo_available ?payload_unit.

Thus loading payload locks origin availability (makes it locked) and occupies node, and links payload.

Thus after loading, origin_availability_locked becomes true (as desired). Also origin_node_occupied true.

